cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "membrane-brain: a brain-shaped toy for a holographic-membrane associative memory with a refusal gate (synthetic)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/membrane-brain"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Synthetic, stdlib-only Python toy: 128 seeded neurons in two ellipses,
  four stored wave fields, a one-shot outer-product associative memory
  and a frozen refusal gate. It is not a brain, not neuroscience and not
  a medical or clinical tool. The repository documents measured behaviour
  and limits, including negative results.
keywords:
  - "synthetic"
  - "toy-model"
  - "associative-memory"
  - "reproducible"
  - "python"
